{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1480","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1480","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1480\",\"parent_revision\":\"d67a168e6e93219c9d8b95a78026981b046035d79c3586299b2801056aa633b9\",\"root_revision\":\"d67a168e6e93219c9d8b95a78026981b046035d79c3586299b2801056aa633b9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`sam_list` accepts a `search` parameter but `_plan_matches_search` checks only 3 fields: `feature`, `description`, `goal`. Task titles, body content, and acceptance criteria are not searched. Agents looking for a plan by a task name must fetch all plans via `sam_read` and scan manually.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `plan_dict[\\\"tasks\\\"]` available as `list[dict]` | AVAILABLE | `sam_schema/server.py:388`, `core/models.py:295` |\\n| Task text fields accessible in `task` dict | AVAILABLE | `sam_schema/core/models.py:118\u2013203` |\\n| `_plan_matches_search` is a pure function | AVAILABLE | `sam_schema/server.py:297\u2013314` |\\n| Task fields not iterated in current search | MISSING | Confirmed \u2014 function body checks only 3 fields |\\n| Docstring field list inaccurate | MISSING | `sam_list` docstring repeats 3-field limitation |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail \u2014 search scope is narrower than the data available in the already-serialised plan dict\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Must change:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `_plan_matches_search` (lines 297\u2013314), `sam_list` docstring (lines 331\u2013362)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEvery `sam_list` call with a `search` string that matches task content but not plan-level fields returns zero results. Failure mode is silent \u2014 no error, just missing results. Callers: any orchestrator that calls `sam_list(search=...)` to locate a plan by task name or AC keyword.\\n\\n**Backward compatibility:** fully additive \u2014 existing matches continue to match; new matches appear for previously-missed plans. No API surface change.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**P2** \u2014 false-negative search results: agents conclude no relevant plan exists and fall back to loading all plans via `sam_read`. This worsens context usage per search.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Agents locate plans by task title or acceptance criteria in one call\\n- Eliminates fallback pattern: `sam_list` \u2192 zero results \u2192 iterate all plans via `sam_read`\\n- No API change \u2014 same parameters, broader match semantics\\n- Early-return on plan-level match preserved \u2014 task iteration only runs when plan fields didn't match\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `_plan_matches_search` iterates `plan_dict.get(\\\"tasks\\\", [])` and checks needle against at minimum: `title`, `body`, `description`, `acceptance_criteria` per task\\n- [ ] A plan whose task `title` contains the search term is returned even when `feature`, `description`, and `goal` do not match\\n- [ ] A plan whose task `acceptance_criteria` contains the search term is returned\\n- [ ] A plan with no matching task content and no matching plan-level fields is not returned (no regression on true-negative)\\n- [ ] `sam_list` tool docstring updated to list all searched fields\\n- [ ] Early-return preserved: task loop only runs when plan-level loop returned no match\\n- [ ] Unit tests cover: match on plan-level field only, match on task `title` only, match on task `acceptance_criteria` only, no match anywhere (excluded), match in both (included, not duplicated)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**NARROW** \u2014 single function, ~10 lines of code change, one file. Docstring update in same file. Tests extend existing `sam_list` test fixture. Under 1 hour implementation + tests.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using SAM for plan management**, I want **`sam_list` to search task content (title, body, acceptance criteria) in addition to plan-level fields** so that **agents can locate plans by task keywords without loading every plan individually**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research finding \u2014 mcp-ux-improvements-20260404.md, validated mcp-ux-improvements-validation-20260404.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Groomed**: 2026-04-09\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current Behavior Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`_plan_matches_search` (`sam_schema/server.py:297\u2013314`):\\n\\n```python\\nfor field in (\\\"feature\\\", \\\"description\\\", \\\"goal\\\"):\\n    value = plan_dict.get(field)\\n    if isinstance(value, str) and needle in value.lower():\\n        return True\\nreturn False\\n```\\n\\n`plan_dict` is `Plan.model_dump(mode=\\\"json\\\")`. It contains `plan_dict[\\\"tasks\\\"]` \u2014 a `list[dict]` where each dict is a `Task.model_dump()`. Task text fields available but not checked: `title`, `body`, `description`, `objective`, `requirements`, `constraints`, `acceptance_criteria`, `verification_steps`, `context_notes`, `expected_outputs` (`sam_schema/core/models.py:118\u2013203`).\\n\\nThe `sam_list` tool docstring also states only the 3-field limitation (lines 331\u2013362).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current Behavior (Evidence)\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`_plan_matches_search` (`sam_schema/server.py:297\u2013314`):\\n\\n```python\\nfor field in (\\\"feature\\\", \\\"description\\\", \\\"goal\\\"):\\n    value = plan_dict.get(field)\\n    if isinstance(value, str) and needle in value.lower():\\n        return True\\nreturn False\\n```\\n\\n`plan_dict` is `Plan.model_dump(mode=\\\"json\\\")`. It contains `plan_dict[\\\"tasks\\\"]` \u2014 a `list[dict]` where each dict is a `Task.model_dump()`. Task text fields available but not checked: `title`, `body`, `description`, `objective`, `requirements`, `constraints`, `acceptance_criteria`, `verification_steps`, `context_notes`, `expected_outputs` (`sam_schema/core/models.py:118\u2013203`).\\n\\nThe `sam_list` tool docstring also states only the 3-field limitation (lines 331\u2013362).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nChange confined to `_plan_matches_search` in `sam_schema/server.py`. After the existing 3-field loop, add:\\n\\n```python\\nTASK_SEARCH_FIELDS = (\\\"title\\\", \\\"body\\\", \\\"description\\\", \\\"acceptance_criteria\\\")\\n\\nfor task in plan_dict.get(\\\"tasks\\\", []):\\n    if not isinstance(task, dict):\\n        continue\\n    for field in TASK_SEARCH_FIELDS:\\n        value = task.get(field)\\n        if isinstance(value, str) and needle in value.lower():\\n            return True\\nreturn False\\n```\\n\\nDefine `TASK_SEARCH_FIELDS` as a module-level constant so the searched set is explicit and easy to extend. Additional fields (`objective`, `requirements`, `constraints`, `verification_steps`) are safe to include \u2014 decision on exact set should be aligned with the issue author. The minimum viable set is `title` + `body` + `description` + `acceptance_criteria`.\\n\\nUpdate the `sam_list` docstring `search` parameter description to enumerate the actual checked fields at both plan-level and task-level.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"51015c01376b236531fca2c293ffb9c82ad8921397987dd801abbf3ad791cbde\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdrecQ\"}"}